+# Solution: Prompt Caching Fix for Memory Writes
+
+## Cause of the Issue
+Previously, [`build_system()`](file:///tmp/h-KWzCjd/bot.py#L130-L136) concatenated the static coaching instructions (`INSTRUCTIONS`) and the dynamic per-athlete profile/facts (`athlete_context(a, today)`) into a single text block with a `cache_control` marker:
+
+```python
+def build_system(a, today):
+    text = INSTRUCTIONS + "\n\n" + athlete_context(a, today)
+    return [{"type": "text", "text": text, "cache_control": {"type": "ephemeral"}}]
+```
+
+Because Anthropic prompt caching matches exact prefix byte-for-byte, any change to the prompt invalidates the cache for that block and everything downstream. When an athlete shared a durable fact, `save_fact` appended a new item to `athlete.facts`. In the subsequent tool round or message, `athlete_context()` changed, altering the single combined block. This caused a complete cache miss (`cache_creation_input_tokens: ~1000+`, `cache_read_input_tokens: 0`), forcing a full re-computation charge for the entire system prompt including the static instructions.
+
+## Changes Made
+In [`bot.py`](file:///tmp/h-KWzCjd/bot.py):
+1. Separated the system prompt in [`build_system()`](file:///tmp/h-KWzCjd/bot.py#L130-L136) into two distinct content blocks:
+   - A static block containing `INSTRUCTIONS` with `{"cache_control": {"type": "ephemeral"}}`.
+   - A dynamic block containing `athlete_context(a, today)` without cache control.
+
+```python
+def build_system(a, today):
+    # Two blocks: static coaching instructions (cached across all athletes and calls)
+    # followed by dynamic athlete-specific context (profile, facts, date).
+    return [
+        {"type": "text", "text": INSTRUCTIONS, "cache_control": {"type": "ephemeral"}},
+        {"type": "text", "text": athlete_context(a, today)},
+    ]
+```
+
+## Verification
+- Tested structure and types returned by `build_system(a, today)`: verified it returns two blocks, the first containing the exact static instructions with ephemeral cache control, and the second containing the dynamic context.
+- Verified tool execution flow with mocked LLM rounds: confirmed that when `save_fact` executes and modifies athlete facts, the static instructions block remains unchanged with its cache marker intact across rounds.
